# GitHub PR workflow

Default branch is `main`. Do not commit, push, or open work directly on `main`.

## Branch

- Create a focused branch from `main`: `feat/…`, `fix/…`, `chore/…`, `docs/…`, `refactor/…`, `test/…`.
- Keep the PR small and about one purpose.

## Commits

- Conventional commits only (`feat: …`, `chore(scope): …`). Lefthook `commit-msg` runs commitlint.
- Never skip hooks (`--no-verify`). Lefthook also runs Biome on staged files.

## Pull request

When the work is ready (or the user asks to open a PR):

1. Push the branch (`git push -u origin HEAD` if it has no upstream).
2. Open the PR with `gh pr create`. Base is `main`.
3. Title and body must follow `.github/pull_request_template.md` — same layout for humans and agents. Pass `--body` via a HEREDOC. Fill every section; do not leave placeholders.
4. Return the PR URL when done.

Do not merge the PR or force-push `main` unless the user explicitly asks.
